    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "According to the UK Health Security Agency, 5,258 heat-related deaths were recorded in the United Kingdom in 2026, the highest on record and above the previous record set in 2022.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-24:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:09Z",
      "text": "Parts of the United Kingdom were severely affected by a series of record-breaking heatwaves, which formed the western edge of a wider run of extreme heat across Western and Central Europe.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1387581085:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:18Z",
      "text": "The events are located in the United Kingdom, as the reports place them.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-24:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:26Z",
      "text": "The heatwaves are dated to 2026, and the record shows they began on 22 May 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q140157671:P585",
        "wd:Q140157671:P580"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:36Z",
      "text": "The story was reported by Reuters.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-24:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-24T00:00:44Z",
      "text": "This explainer draws on Wikipedia, its current events and article revisions, Wikimedia pageview counts, and Wikidata, and each statement is tied to the evidence behind it.",
